  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The number of endothermic process/es from the following is _______.</p><p>A. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>B.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>Cl</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>C. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>D. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>E. Dissolution of ammonium chloride in water</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The decomposition reactions are endothermic reactions. The reactions&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>Cl</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;are decomposition reactions. The heat vaporisation is an endothermic reaction. Hence, the conversion of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mfenced><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow></mrow></mover><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is endothermic process. The heat of combustion is an exothermic process. The heat involved in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#10230;</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;is heat of combustion.&nbsp;The dissolution of ammonium chloride in water is an endothermic process. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi>Cl</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><msubsup><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>Cl</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
